    "narrative": "The standout play for LawDog today is undoubtedly **Jung Hoo Lee**, who secures a score of 65.65. Positioned in the heart of the order at #3, **Jung Hoo Lee** benefits from a massive situational upgrade against Jose Cabrera. With Cabrera\u2019s xERA sitting at a vulnerable 5.16 and the platoon advantage shifting in favor of **Jung Hoo Lee**, his profile is optimized for a high-floor performance, carrying the team's offensive expectations into the \"Strong\" start territory. Conversely, **Daulton Varsho** (53.15) holds significant value despite facing the elite Gerrit Cole. While Cole\u2019s 3.39 xERA acts as a natural anchor on output, **Daulton Varsho** maintains marginal start status due to his advantageous platoon split and projected #5 slot, keeping him ahead of the volatility typically associated with top-tier pitching matchups.\n\nThe bottom half of the lineup presents a tighter squeeze, with **Dylan Beavers** (48.63) and **Yainer Diaz** (42.36) both hovering in the marginal category. **Dylan Beavers** finds himself in a neutral spot, but the lack of a clear, favorable matchup pushes him into a \"start only if needed\" territory. **Yainer Diaz** is the most precarious of our active starters; facing Gerrit Cole while batting in the #8 hole forces his score down significantly, despite a solid base projection. We are monitoring the lineups for both **Dylan Beavers** and **Yainer Diaz** closely, as any drop in their batting order would likely trigger a benching to protect our remaining game caps.\n\nRegarding roster availability, the bench is largely stagnant due to scheduled team off-days for key contributors like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Bryce Harper**, while **Will Smith** remains sidelined on the IL. With the rest of the squad\u2014including high-upside options like **Lawrence Butler**, **Justin Crawford**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Zack Gelof**, **Luis Arraez**, 